learnings:
  - The cross-package import (CLI core → paradigm-mcp utils) was the make-or-break feasibility question; confirmed it works via the established relative-path precedent (core/habits/evaluator.ts:11) + tsup noExternal bundling. Verified before committing a builder, avoiding a wasted round.
  - 'Loop-closure for a new execution path is cheap once settlement exists: the bridge only has to create epic+child tasks and call completeTask on them; the settlement hook inside updateTask does the rest. The primitive (settlement-on-terminal-with-parent) generalizes across execution worlds.'
